# k11: the plain wmma kernel, tile loads by ordinary vectorized ld/st;
# ceildiv trips because the K loop is `for (k = 0; k < K; k += 16)`.
# Each CTA declares 8192 B of shared memory; per thread and trip 4096
# tensor flops, 320 B loaded from shared memory, 64 B stored to it and
# at most 64 B of global loads, the kernel's totals' terms in ⌈K/16⌉.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k11/k11.sm_80.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z10hgemm_wmmaILi128ELi128ELi16ELi64ELi64ELi128EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0_( // shared memory 8,192 B/CTA | per thread: flops f32 <= 384; tensor flops f16 4096·⌈param_2/16⌉; global load <= (64·⌈param_2/16⌉ + 256) B, store <= 512 B; shared load 320·⌈param_2/16⌉ B, store 64·⌈param_2/16⌉ B; param load <= 64 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips ⌈param_2/16⌉ | under line 72 | exec ⌈param_2/16⌉/thread{{$}}
